{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic","id":1107405,"title":"Making money with magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-24T12:55:55-07:00","id":1107405,"title":"Making money with magic","content":"I've heard it said on these forums that any mage is just a Ruling spell away from never worrying about money again.<br /> I would like to take this further and explore the various means mages have of using magic to get rich. I would also like to highlight and explore the risks and problems involved in every method.<br /> <br /> I'll write down a few examples myself by Arcana, marred by my limited imagination and knowledge of the gameworld. Please contribute with examples as well. I would very much like to hear of more unique and unexpected ways to make money in this game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Use any magic to become an incredible artist / musician / actor / stage magician</b><br /> This method will draw attention to you very fast. You generally do not want attention as a mage. If you are going this route, hope that you can build up your fame to shield you from sympathetic magic. The only way I see this work is if you restrain your magic to not perform too well and stay below the radar, but this kind of defeats the purpose I'd say.<br /> <br /> <b>Use any magic to augment / enhance / hone your mundane Skills and Attributes, helping you get successful at a day job, albeit not famous</b><br /> An indirect method of using magic to make money. I am not sure if many mages would object to this, at least not the Pentacle. The main problem has to do with laying low. The more successful you are at your job, the more you are likely to play an extremely important role in whatever career or domain you pursue, which will make it more difficult (though not at all impossible) to really stay anonymous.<br /> <br /> <b>Use any magic to steal money</b><br /> Stealing money and valuable artifacts using magic is just a matter of imagination and can be done with any Arcana, but I would expect it is viewed as very petty. You may not need to care about Sleeper law enforcement, but repeatedly commiting crimes using magic is sure to draw the attention of much more capable entities.<br /> <br /> <b>Use any magic to lie, cheat and finagle your way in life</b><br /> This is very similar to the above example, but is more about commiting many small acts of subterfuge and larceny to get specific things you need or want but not to amass lots of money. As long as you keep it discreet and small-scale and do not let other mages find out about your lifestyle I see few problems with it.<br /> <br /> <b>Use Death magic to become a successful medium</b><br /> Mundane fakers make tons of money doing this, using unimpressive tricks. A mage who is actually doing it for real should be quite successful as well. Though, thinking about the way ghosts and anchors work in CofD, Death magic ironically seems to have little utility for a medium, as the typical medium works at a fixed location and the clients come to them. A real necromancer would need to go where the ghosts actually are and could do so for their clients. The necromancer could also use trickery just like a typical medium and augment it by using actual ghosts as part of the show. Both venues would probably be viewed as a serious breach of secrecy and put the necromancer on the watch list for Guardians of the Veil.<br /> <br /> <b>Use Fate magic to guarantee a comfortable life without accidents or misshaps, removing the need for money in the first place</b><br /> I don't see many mages objecting to this as it seems discreet enough and I supposed it is something a typical Fate mage would do. It won't make you rich, but if you have modest ambitions it will serve you well enough.<br /> <br /> <b>Use Fate or Time magic to pick the right lottery ticket</b><br /> There was an entire thread about this (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007901-using-the-time-arcanum-to-win-a-lottery\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-win-a-lottery</a>). A summary of the arguments had it that lottery winners are watched closely by all kinds of interested parties, mundane and magical alike, making it a risky proposition.<br /> <br /> <b>Use Fate or Time magic to pick the right stocks and do the right investments in the stock market</b><br /> I would think the Seers have the stock market firmly under watch and grasp. You would not be able to break into that business in my games without joining them.<br /> <br /> <b>Use Life magic to perform medical miracles</b><br /> If you are doing it as a doctor you risk drawing unwanted attention to yourself. If the miracles are simply <i>too </i>miraculous, dissonance will set in. If you are doing it as a faith healer it might reasonably be easier to get away with it, at least if you are working for the Guardians of the Veil as a cultor. That very position might not net you that much money though.<br /> <br /> <b>Use Life magic to eliminate the need for food, water and sleep</b><br /> A very indirect method. Not to get rich, but definitely to keep expenses down and productivity up. I see no direct problems with this other than risking detachment from what it means to be a human.<br /> <br /> <b>Use Matter or magic to counterfeit money</b><br /> As with any criminal activity, this method is sure to draw attention to the uncareful mage who cannot keep it small-scale. As large amounts of fake money come into circulation in the economy, many interested parties would take notice. Reading the economy for strange disturbances would probably be a Seer specialty, I think.<br /> <br /> <b>Use Matter magic to produce gold and other valuable materials</b><br /> Just like the above post, doing this in a large scale is sure to draw lots of unwanted attention as the global economy constantly keeps tabs on what goods are in circulation on the market. Doing this large scale would of course decrease the value of the goods, but I think the mage has been put out long before it came to that.<br /> <br /> <b>Use Matter Magic to create facilities, equipment, vehicles and other goods so you won't have to buy them with magic</b><br /> As long as the mage can keep it discreet (producing legitimate paperwork for their housing and car for example, and not showing off terribly) I don't think there should be a lot of trouble with this venue.<br /> <br /> <b>Use Prime magic to produce and sell mana to mages</b><br /> Mana does not seem all that scarce and expensive in 2E when any legacy makes a mage into a walking Hallow, but I still see a market for it even if it might be a bit crowded. The biggest problem however that I can see is that mana is the only real currency for mages to begin with, and that trading mana for money is ultimately short-cutting yourself when you could do better things for you by using it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T22:10:51-07:00","id":1107514,"title":"","content":"Going to talk only about direct methods to get money through magic, because just being better at your job is...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://media.riemurasia.net/albumit/mmedia/lp/8kv/hggt/3175/1541991119.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Forces: </b>Matter allows you to control mechanical devices at 1 dots, so it's safe to assume that Forces do the same for electronics at 1-2 dots. So go ask an ATM for some cash.<br /> <b>Prime: </b>No direct methods<br /> <b>Fate:</b> has a spell that gives you [Potency] Resources<br /> <b>Time: </b>Doesn't give money directly, but allows you to stretch resources indefinitely at 3 dots. Eat a sandwich, shifting sands, eat it again. Refill at a hallow, shifting sands, refill again.<br /> <b>Spirit: </b>Summon a spirit, has it influence/possess people to give you money.<br /> <b>Life: </b>Augment your body, steal/earn money.<br /> <b>Matter: </b>Use Shaping and Machine Invisibility to rob banks and ATMs. <br /> <b>Death: </b>use ghosts to possess people. Blackmail people by holding the soul of their grandpa (or theirs) hostage<br /> <b>Mind: </b>come on<br /> <b>Space: </b>Scrying and Break Boundary make you sleuth and criminal extraordinaire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T22:34:05-07:00","id":1107518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1107514#post1107514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Refill at a hallow, shifting sands, refill again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you actually allow that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T22:45:32-07:00","id":1107523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1107518#post1107518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you actually allow that?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's either that, or refund people the mana that was spent in the shifted period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T23:18:39-07:00","id":1107534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1107523#post1107523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's either that, or refund people the mana that was spent in the shifted period.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the shifted period, you either performed an oblation for an hour or cast Channel Mana, and neither option actually allows a full refill without the kinds of contexts in which you'd have the time to top off anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T23:56:22-07:00","id":1107551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1107534#post1107534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the shifted period, you either performed an oblation for an hour or cast Channel Mana, and neither option actually allows a full refill without the kinds of contexts in which you'd have the time to top off anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um. What?<br /> <br /> Variant 1. Mana travels with you.<br /> If this is the case, then you can perform an oblation/drain artefact/drain a familiar, shift back in time, do it again, shift back and have all the mana before you ever did anything.<br /> <br /> Variant 2. Mana doesn't travel back in time. This is explicitly contrary to how Shifting Sands work. But if it wasn't then spending mana and then using Shifting Sands should give mana back. Useful for pumping mana into information gathering spells.<br /> <br /> Variant 3. Mana is a cosmic constant and when you Shifting Sands the drained hallow remains drained. In this scenario mages should spontaneously lose mana all the time because some Acanthus somewhere Shifting Sandsed after they drained a hallow/cast a spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T00:12:46-07:00","id":1107557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1107551#post1107551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um. What?</div> </div> </div> </div>Variant <i>This Has Nothing To Do With Your Mana Total</i>. If you can spare multiple iterations of an hour to do an Oblation at a Hallow the multiple times it would take to gather the free Mana the Hallow generates, you can spare an hour engaged in low-level Praxes to gradually refill your Mana total. If you can personally cast both Shifting Sands and Channel Mana, you have at least three dots in two Arcana and very probably also have rotes of one or both of the effects and thus are running a rather more specific or experienced build and therefore have bigger fish to fry than topping off your safety margin.<br /> <br /> The stress point of Mage's fuel economy is not &quot;I have a spare hour and access to time travel and a Hallow.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is explicitly contrary to how Shifting Sands work. </div> </div> </div>It isn't, actually \u2014 &quot;spent Mana is not recovered&quot; does not imply &quot;gained Mana is not lost.&quot; The nearest point of ambiguity is whether Channel Mana counts as a spell cast on something other than yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T07:01:59-07:00","id":1107622,"title":"","content":"I would argue Death wouldn't make you a more successful medium. People don't want the truth, they want pretty soothing lies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T09:15:13-07:00","id":1107654,"title":"","content":"Not to mention ghosts are twisted versions of the people they once were, Virtue/Vice flip and all that.<br /> <br /> Shifting the Odds straight up gives you Resources so that would be a fairly easy way to hit Resources 5 whenever you want. Sure it only lasts as long as the spell, but you can just do it over and over again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T09:40:30-07:00","id":1107664,"title":"","content":"Rather than make money using ghosts as a medium, you could go the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Necroscope\" target=\"_blank\">Necroscope</a> way. Many of the worlds dead are authors, artists, academics and so forth. One could use them to continue their work and profit off of it. Since you can make a ghost of a living person you wouldn't even necessarily need to find a dead one.<br /> <br /> Others might have knowledge of hidden treasures. Find the lost Axis gold or mineral veins or petroleum deposits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T16:27:04-07:00","id":1107791,"title":"","content":"Praxis and ES makes refilling mana trivial, whats the need for shifting sands and oblations?<br /> <br /> So Colocation and sympathy to any location with valuables means you can steal them at your leisure. You can pinch it, pawn it, pinch it from pawn shop, replace it. Only having to deal with a pawn shop thats in another state/country cos ya know Space.<br /> <br /> Matter 3's crucible can make things more valuable easily, get shit, make it worth more, sell it, profit.<br /> <br /> Forces 3 and platonic form can make stuff that looks non magical, which you can sell, profit.<br /> <br /> Most of the stuff mages will have to worry about is what happens when the spells runs out. But give your spells a reasonable duration and its not your problem if stuff vanishes weeks later is it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T17:08:10-07:00","id":1107813,"title":"","content":"A couple off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> Life: A knowing magic to find valuable forage items like truffles or furbearers<br /> Matter: Run an exceptionally profitable scrapyard/foundry <br /> Prime: Knowing if someone is lying to you would be spectacularly useful when flipping cars, houses, thrift shop finds, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T18:08:20-07:00","id":1107831,"title":"","content":"Time 4 can sorta give money directly if you Rewrite History to rearrange your merits to resources 5 and buy stuff during its duration. Not quite sure the specifics of what happens when the spell ends? The money came from a alternate timeline so doesnt vanish?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T20:27:23-07:00","id":1107865,"title":"","content":"<b>Life:</b> Use it to generate valuable tissues and possibly organs. Blood isn't the only thing you can donate that can make you a decent chunk of change.<br /> <b>Spirit:</b> There are an insane amount of Influences that could make you money. However Spirit 1 -Coaxing the Spirit and ask an ATM if it wouldn't be a dear and spit out some cash. Same goes with cars if you don't mind being a car thief. Even riskier would be to use it on a service (Like say some Dating App) to give you personal information about someone which you can use to blackmail someone or just get useful info.<br /> <b>Prime:</b> There's plenty of options here as well. Create an object out of Tass for selling, doubly useful if it's something easy to lose like jewelry.<br /> <b>Matter:</b> The easiest way would be to go to a junkyard or other place that sells or has broken/damaged good and just magic them new. The spell is Lasting so you don't have too much to worry about and if anyone asks you have a garage or whatever.<br /> <b>Mind:</b> Blackmail/Command someone to give you money. Pretty blatant but not terrible. Mind 2 - Telepathy, go to a casino and read the dealer's mind. Easiest with games like Blackjack.<br /> <b>Fate:</b> Way too easy.<br /> <b>Time:</b> Shifting Sands back every hour at a casino until you hit it big. Time 1 - Perfect Timing would let you win any games of chance where timing matters. Time 1 - Divination works on things like 'Will this X win?'<br /> <b>Forces:</b> Insurance fraud could be a thing here for various valuables. There's always the ATM trick to hack it for money. Straight up manipulate something like a roulette wheel or pickpocket people from a distance.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12824-bloodyquill","name":"Bloodyquill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T21:01:08-07:00","id":1107874,"title":"","content":"Id say Matter 1's remote control with the reach for complex objects covers ATM's. Forces isnt really the goto for controlling electrical devices anymore is it? Sure you can control the power inside it, heat n whatnot but hows that going to get a atm to spit cash out just from controling a force?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T23:25:55-07:00","id":1107915,"title":"","content":"What do you think you are doing when pressing the buttons then? You could do it with Forces, you could do it with Matter too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T00:31:14-07:00","id":1107925,"title":"","content":"You cant just walk up to a atm and push some buttons (without a valid card) for it to shower you in money. I just dont see what forces would be doing to make a atm machine spit out money at you. Using forces to control anything electronic and computers etc was used often in 1e im just not sure thats still relevant in 2e. I get that you could probably use forces to alter data on hard drives via EM fields or erase it via magnetism etc. I just think matter has now got alot of stuff for controlling machines now even electronic ones over forces.<br /> <br /> An easy example of what i mean is &quot;Invisibility to Machines&quot; was a forces 2 effect in the free council book is now a matter effect in 2e. I can see things like reading data of a hard drive also using matter, (maybe forces too if powered though). Just my thoughts, other peoples opinions might vary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T01:23:52-07:00","id":1107940,"title":"","content":"Electronic data falls under Forces purview. <br /> <br /> Of course you would need a card, but magic is taking care of that, let's discuss in good faith, shall we? <br /> <br /> Also, Arcana overlap a lot on purpose, you could do that Invisible to Machines effect as a Veiling of Forces just as fine.<br /> <br /> Edit: my point is that is never a question of either or, you can do the same thing with multiple approaches","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T23:02:31-07:00","id":1111171,"title":"","content":"Forces &amp; ATM is easy. Computers &amp; programming pretty much boils down to 1s &amp; 0s, true &amp; false. All you need to do is trip the &quot;eject $20 bills&quot; logic gate, and there you go.<br /> <br /> I feel like Shifting Sands @ a casino would be too great a paradox risk -- but I am probably still stuck in MtAw-1. Instead, I'd suggest penny stocks &amp; simple divination. &quot;Will this stock double today?&quot; No? Move on to the next symbol. Alternatively, Black Jack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/793-phil","name":"phil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T08:04:12-07:00","id":1111269,"title":"","content":"Prime is rather simple. Become a broker of magic itself, and get other people to make money for you in exchange for drams of tass. Create enchanted items and sell for large favors. Be a professional geomancer and align ley lines for fun and profit: it arguably requires an entire character concept, but being a supernatural landscape architect has to have big bucks involved in there somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1516-solarious","name":"Solarious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T10:47:08-07:00","id":1111341,"title":"","content":"If you want to sell Tass you'd want it in the form of food for those without Prime, and preferably food that won't spoil. I'm thinking the Adamantine Arrow in charge of a military surplus store selling Tass to other mages in the form of MREs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T11:57:57-07:00","id":1111373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1111341#post1111341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to sell Tass you'd want it in the form of food for those without Prime, and preferably food that won't spoil. I'm thinking the Adamantine Arrow in charge of a military surplus store selling Tass to other mages in the form of MREs.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could also just charge people to break their Tass into mana for them. Charge for your services rather than your product.<br /> <br /> That's something you can do with any Arcanum, for the record. No matter what your specialty is, there's probably another local mage (or mortal!) who has use of it. I'd imagine charging $$ cash money for it (as opposed to bartering favors, knowledge and/or magical objects) is seen as a little crass, but you gotta do what you gotta do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T11:17:28-07:00","id":1111726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1111373#post1111373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could also just charge people to break their Tass into mana for them. Charge for your services rather than your product.<br /> <br /> That's something you can do with any Arcanum, for the record. No matter what your specialty is, there's probably another local mage (or mortal!) who has use of it. I'd imagine charging $$ cash money for it (as opposed to bartering favors, knowledge and/or magical objects) is seen as a little crass, but you gotta do what you gotta do.</div> </div> </div> </div>With simple praxis spells regaining mana is trivial, i dont think there would be much money in selling Tass/Mana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T11:46:38-07:00","id":1111751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1111726#post1111726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With simple praxis spells regaining mana is trivial, i dont think there would be much money in selling Tass/Mana?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which spells exactly? Surely it's not <i>so</i> easy that you can't even get a fresh Disciple or two to fork over a couple bucks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T12:11:44-07:00","id":1111764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1111751#post1111751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which spells exactly? Surely it's not <i>so</i> easy that you can't even get a fresh Disciple or two to fork over a couple bucks?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the effects you can choose when getting an Exceptional Success on spellcasting is to refund all Mana spent on the spell plus one additional Mana. Praxes makes it very easy to get Exceptionals so you can top your Mana pool quite easy. Same goes with Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T12:43:18-07:00","id":1111782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1111764#post1111764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the effects you can choose when getting an Exceptional Success on spellcasting is to refund all Mana spent on the spell plus one additional Mana. Praxes makes it very easy to get Exceptionals so you can top your Mana pool quite easy. Same goes with Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeeeah, to me that sounds more like RAW abuse than an inherent fact about magic that needs to be taken into account when answering worldbuilding questions. I don't know about you guys, but I would instantly veto any attempt to do that. Lazily casting a spell over and over shouldn't require rolls, much less allow you to achieve Exceptional Successes.<br /> <br /> e: in fact it defeats the entire purpose of an &quot;exceptional&quot; success, not to mention destroys the entire Willpower and Mana economy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","user":"Terrorforge","date":". 07-05-2017, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T14:24:56-07:00","id":1111810,"title":"","content":"It's working as intended though if it tempts players to use their Praxis more frequently than other spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T14:28:53-07:00","id":1111811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1111810#post1111810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's working as intended though if it tempts players to use their Praxis more frequently than other spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but there's a big difference between &quot;more frequently than other spells&quot; or even &quot;at every opportunity&quot; and &quot;several times in a row for no other reason than to fish for the side effects of an Exceptional Success&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T14:30:30-07:00","id":1111814,"title":"","content":"I agree about Mana. Especially considering that another alternative is taking a Condition relating to the spellcasting and that most STs probably say no to handing out Conditions when not casting spells for an actual purpose.<br /> The Willpower gain is by design, though. Magic feels great and indulging in that grants mages Willpower similar to a Vice. You could restrict it to once per scene if you'd like, though, just like Vices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T14:45:46-07:00","id":1111821,"title":"","content":"I don't think crit fishing for any resource by performing pointless tasks over and over is by design. If nothing else I don't think that repeating something without really trying to accomplish anything involves making the kind of effort that could propel you into an Exceptional Success.<br /> <br /> That said, it's actually an interesting angle. I might allow that, with the provision that it's an Act of Hubris. Casting repeatedly just for the thrill of it is in fact explicitly called out as something Mad Ones do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T09:36:02-07:00","id":1112156,"title":"","content":"I'd like to contribute to this thread but I have limited knowledge of 2nd Edition mage and my ideas aren't about getting rich per se... My ideas are things my PCs have done to avoid needing money any more. Once you live the life of a mage, you start to loose connection to things like a mundane job, but you still have bills to pay, right? I think that any of my ideas can be converted from 1st Edition to 2nd Edition by people in the know.<br /> <br /> <b>Forces, ATMs, and other things</b> -- This has been mentioned and is being discussed right now. In 1st Edition is a was a simple matter to have a universal password for any electronic device. With an ATM this works on two levels (or one) in that you are telling the computer that to access an account with the right PIN and relinquish money to you. Fallen World ethics might tell you that this is wrong and it's stealing. Supernal logic might tell you that money is just a symbol representing the energy needed to get things done. My Obrimos character would have never done this. My Acanthus character did this whenever it was necessary.<br /> <br /> Also, having a place to stay is a snap because hotels all use electronic locks. You can gain access to any room and stay as long as you want. You will want to be aware of when the room will be booked so you don't get caught, but it's really easy to just explain yourself. Someone (not you) made a mistake and this room is taken. Or you can use other magic, Time and Fate, to know which rooms will be available and for how long and then just schedule your squatting rights accordingly.<br /> <br /> Forces (or 2nd Edition Matter) makes it a simple matter to avoid being detected by artificial means. Cameras, motion detectors, etc are not going to capture your presence. So you can avoid getting caught as long as people don't see you.<br /> <br /> <b>Food and stuff</b> -- Life and Matter magic make it really simple to have plenty of food. You can create edible things out of non-edible things if you want or you can be a master gardener, growing enough food to feed an entire family with only the simplest of resources.<br /> <br /> <b>Gasoline</b> -- If you've got a motorcycle or something like that, maybe even an electrical generator, you can collect rainwater and transmute it into fuel with a Matter 2 spell and then use it power your stuff so you never have to worry about paying for gasoline again. You have to make sure you extend the duration long enough to use to fuel, otherwise you will have water in your gas tank and that won't be good for your engines. Also, if you don't mind stealing, Matter 2 makes it exceptionally easy to siphon gasoline from other sources and move it to your container or what not.<br /> <br /> <b>Lottery Tickets and other things</b> -- My Acanthus character only did things like this for emergency cash. It's too time consuming to spend all your time finding winning tickets and scratching them off. It's much easier to use your Fate magic to cast a spell that give you great luck and synchronicity all day long. You also catch the bus, you're never late, you find 20 bucks, kind strangers pay for your lunch, etc.<br /> <br /> If you're single, only having to worry about taking care of yourself, and you can find four walls and a roof, magic makes it easy to have all the basic necessities. Your clothes are always clean and new and fresh. You have easy access to food and fuel and heat (a single candle could heat an entire house). And if you're trying to remain anonymous, you can hide your presence pretty well, too. People might just see an empty apartment or an abandoned house.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T09:38:11-07:00","id":1112157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1112156#post1112156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Food and stuff</b> -- Life and Matter magic make it really simple to have plenty of food. You can create edible things out of non-edible things if you want or you can be a master gardener, growing enough food to feed an entire family with only the simplest of resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that's true, a more money-oriented strategy would involve drugs. A Life mage could easily boost manufacturing and product, even on a small personal scale.<br /> <br /> That's ignoring the money potential in 'snake-oil salesman' type schemes or more legal pharmaceuticals. One of the Silver Ladder Reaper Legacies started out as snake-oil hucksters, if I recall correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-06-2017, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T09:50:19-07:00","id":1112165,"title":"","content":"In 2e, transforming one thing into another is universally the purview of the Practice of Weaving, which is available to those with a rating of 4 or above in the relevant Arcanum. So no infinite gas for Apprentices, unfortunately. Life at that level is at least useful in as far as the spell Body Control lets the mage reduce her need for nutrients substantially.<br /> <br /> It's also worth remembering that usually no one mage has access to every kind of magic. Almost any Moros can keep her gear in perfect order, but she's going to have to work for her food. Almost any Thyrsus can live off the land indefinitely, but can't summon $20 out of nowhere when she needs to go buy a burner phone. Yet another good reason to form cabals, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T10:28:27-07:00","id":1112190,"title":"","content":"Weaving is a 3 dot effect, I believe you're actually referring to Patterning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T10:32:44-07:00","id":1112196,"title":"","content":"Yeah, my bad. I was thinking of Patterning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T11:01:19-07:00","id":1112220,"title":"","content":"I <i>hate </i>to mention this, but being a Murder Hobo is a trope in the Chronicles of Darkness games, and a Death Mage would be particularly good at it. It's a bit like Breaking Bad Walter White's Problem Solving Flow-chart but replacing cook with murder.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://i.chzbgr.com/full/7580388352/hB3B568B2/\" target=\"_blank\">Image</a></div> <br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Yes... I know that puts &quot;Kill Them&quot; and murder as two steps in the same line, that just explains that killing enemies is separate from the casual murder of strangers and/or &quot;friends&quot; that is normal for the murder hobo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-06-2017, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T11:10:36-07:00","id":1112229,"title":"","content":"Eh. The way money works, most of someone's assets aren't going to fall out of their pocket in dollar form when they die.<br /> <br /> Just like you can target stores and banks and take their money or rearrange their assets to your benefits, you can go after criminals and others who have large amounts of hard currency laying around. But even then, Death is unnecessary, as every Arcana can kill people, and with other Arcana you can find other ways to get the money. Like with Spirit you could do the werewolf thing, just go into the Hisil and take the money from there.<br /> <br /> In the end though it just goes into Aristarkos' 'Use any magic to steal money,' from their first post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T15:23:10-07:00","id":1112374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1112229#post1112229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Use any magic to steal money,'</div> </div> </div> </div>Less stealing &quot;Money&quot; and more living like a hobo that moves into the house/RV/car of their victim, eat their food and generally treat life like a Grand Theft Auto game because they're psychotic (The character, the player may or may not be maladjusted). I mean the type of person to whom money is mostly meaningless because they'll just kill whomever stops them from taking what they want. You know, the standard D&amp;D party.<br /> <br /> I hate to mention it because I've had players who joined my game for a session or two who played that way, and that was unpleasant. There are NPCs in the setting who indeed live that way according to canon, but choosing a play style when that that seriously strains the suspension of disbelief that people willingly spend time with such a &quot;person&quot; when that isn't consented to by the group is not playing well with others Out of Character.<br /> <br /> I mention the Death Arcanum because of how good it is at cleaning up the mess of that lifestyle. The corpses, the ghosts, and the physical trace evidence are all neatly handled under one umbrella.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-06-2017, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T15:54:57-07:00","id":1112388,"title":"","content":"Acanthus have a pretty easy way of doing it: Cast a Fate spell on a rich person such that, should they die, you inherit a large part of their fortune. Then use Fate magic to arrange an &quot;accident.&quot; And you're set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T19:46:35-07:00","id":1112464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1112388#post1112388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">inherit a large part of their fortune.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a particularly gruesome Fate spell that grants Resources. Not quite murder hobo material as it implies settling into attachments gained by the inheritance, and caring about anything isn't murder hobo modus operandi. Murder hobos are alluded to in Space about mages that scrub their spacial sympathetic ties to remove &quot;weaknesses&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Back on topic:</b><br /> Using spirits, ghosts or goetia to extort money like a supernatural protection racket, matching the Ephemeral being to be the most difficult for the extorted party to deal with, Goetia for Uratha, spirits for Sin-eaters and any ephemeral being that doesn't Materialize for vampires.<br /> Anything could just ruin mundane mortal lives of the being' s bane is obscure enough.<br /> <br /> Supernatural dread and being &quot;protected&quot; by bogus charms/ wards which are really you just not ordering the assault on their lives and sanity is not theft and can be very profitable, both monetarily and in favors. It is all about picking a victim that can't deal with what you can control to harass them, and the bonus is, if you play it right you can look like a savior instead of an extortionist. Being assailed by an unseen intangible foe which you have no idea about its capacities or how it works is rightly terrifying, even to big bad tough guys with supernatural power that just so happen to have a blind spot to what's harrying them. Remember Twilight isn't a place, it's a set of frequencies of being and just because you can see some frequencies doesn't mean you can deal with others.<br /> <br /> Mages are very good at providing out of context foes against those that displeased them, three of the five paths have the option without resorting to non-ruling Arcanum, and Supernal or Abyssal beings, if they choose their targets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-07-2017, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T02:06:50-07:00","id":1120706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1112388#post1112388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Acanthus have a pretty easy way of doing it: Cast a Fate spell on a rich person such that, should they die, you inherit a large part of their fortune. Then use Fate magic to arrange an &quot;accident.&quot; And you're set.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would the inheritance simply go to the Mage in this case? Is the bureaucratic machinery manipulated to somehow go to the mage instead of the family or relatives? How would this not prompt some pretty confused relatives to investigate just where the money went?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T02:45:02-07:00","id":1120711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1120706#post1120706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would the inheritance simply go to the Mage in this case? Is the bureaucratic machinery manipulated to somehow go to the mage instead of the family or relatives? How would this not prompt some pretty confused relatives to investigate just where the money went?</div> </div> </div> </div>Strings of Fate, Divine Intervention, Forge Destiny, etc are all pretty obviously geared toward making you the beneficiary of a rich man's will the kind of thing that's not only possible, but likely. Just cast on your Daddy Warbucks (How do you think Annie got so lucky?).<br /> <br /> Sure, the relatives might investigate, but that's basically just plot fuel and not actually a barrier to accomplishing the goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 07-26-2017, 05:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T03:34:49-07:00","id":1120721,"title":"","content":"How much Forces is needed to manipulate electronic banking into having a non-depletable bank account? or failing that access to any specific account with a flick of one's wrist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T08:45:11-07:00","id":1120828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1120721#post1120721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much Forces is needed to manipulate electronic banking into having a non-depletable bank account? or failing that access to any specific account with a flick of one's wrist?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like you should be able to make an ATM pop out cash or a card reader go &quot;yes, absolutely&quot; without even charging an account with just Forces 1 Compelling; that would just require you to manipulate the electronics in front of you to do something they are naturally capable of.<br /> <br /> Enchanting a bank account to always have money in it would be trickier, but it would allow anyone with the right card and PIN to withdraw cash without the use of magic. I don't think you can cast spells on conceptual things like &quot;my bank account&quot;, but would rather have to cast on the physical storage media/computer that handles the bank transactions. It would probably be a relatively simple Forces 2 Ruling spell, but unless you find the server farm and break in you would have to cast sympathetically and with a lot of factors, possibly targeting several locations depending on how the network is set up. You could presumably Borrow Threads the connection between the relevant card and the account it's connected to - unless you're of the opinion that people form sympathetic links with objects but objects don't form links with each other, which some people are.<br /> <br /> Alternatively you could cast a large-scale Compelling (Ruling?) spell on every relevant device in a particular area that makes them not charge the specific account when the card is used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T13:10:07-07:00","id":1120983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1111341#post1111341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to sell Tass you'd want it in the form of food for those without Prime, and preferably food that won't spoil. I'm thinking the Adamantine Arrow in charge of a military surplus store selling Tass to other mages in the form of MREs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd infuse water into Tass and just sell bottled water. Alternately, if I wanted to launder the money a bit more, I'd sell wine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T13:24:49-07:00","id":1120989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1120983#post1120983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd infuse water into Tass and just sell bottled water. Alternately, if I wanted to launder the money a bit more, I'd sell wine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because why oh why would you inflict the horror of MREs into anyone? Am I right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T13:45:55-07:00","id":1121004,"title":"","content":"Actually, laundering the money is probably something that should be discussed. Because, no matter what method the Mage is using to make money, odds are that they don't have a legit paper trail for it afterwards. So, if they want to be able to use their wads of cash, they need to find some kind of method they can use to make their money look legit.<br /> <br /> Granted, some mages might not find cops and IRS agents scary, but I'd imagine that the Seers and the Veil have people in law enforcement who keep an eye out for &quot;weird windfalls&quot; and things that seem like people are making money &quot;like magic.&quot; So, finding a legit method to hide your money is probably just as important as the ability to get it in the first place.<br /> <br /> From what people have said so far, it seems like Fate and Matter are the best Arcana to get money &quot;legitimately.&quot; Fate means you're just lucky, so anything you need tends to come to you when you need it, so money isn't really an issue (but if it was, you could get that too). Matter means you can directly manipulate the symbols of weath, from becoming the best prospector ever at Matter 1, using Shaping to make amazing sculptures at Matter 2, or using Crucible to make a necklace shine with worth at Matter 3. All of those are reasonably legit and, as long as you keep the &quot;lucky breaks&quot; in the fairly plausible range, you should be ok.<br /> <br /> For pretty much anything else, you'll want some kind of money laundry. From fiction, I've been given to understand that owning a Fitness Center, Restaurant, Bar, or other high traffic/high volume business is a good way to have a plausible source for that money. Basically you just report that you do 150% more business than you actually do or that your markup is higher than than it actually is. Alternately, ebay and other online auction sites or online stores could work if you have enough &quot;straw buyers.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T13:53:11-07:00","id":1121008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1121004#post1121004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, laundering the money is probably something that should be discussed. Because, no matter what method the Mage is using to make money, odds are that they don't have a legit paper trail for it afterwards. So, if they want to be able to use their wads of cash, they need to find some kind of method they can use to make their money look legit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on your lifestyle, I suppose. If you have a regular job and life you can launder it through that. But you might not even need to bother, as many things you might use the money for you could just get through other means.<br /> <br /> If you just want 'things,' for instance, you can just go into stores and walk out with them, using magic so that no one's the wiser.<br /> <br /> If you want to buy and maintain security for a huge parcel of land to make sure no one accidentally stumbles upon the dangerous verge within, you might need your name on things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T14:49:05-07:00","id":1121032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1121004#post1121004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, finding a legit method to hide your money is probably just as important as the ability to get it in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>This exactly why I started the thread; any mage can make lots of money, but it's more difficult to hide their activities from interested parties. I can imagine that Seers, especially those serving Mammon, keep close observation of any and all economic activities to detect if anyone screws with it. This would be an excellent way to find recruits, since screwing the system to get rich without caring about the consequences would be the first thing many new orderless and uninitiated mages would do, mages who are much easier to lure to their side.<br /> <br /> It also serves as an explanation as to how the Seers can offer so much material rewards: they rule the system and so can simply supply their servants luxuries and wealth without anyone stopping them,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 07-26-2017, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T14:58:26-07:00","id":1121036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1112165#post1112165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Almost any Moros can keep her gear in perfect order, but she's going to have to work for her food.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, &quot;work&quot;. Fate is always cited as the big &quot;casino&quot; Arcanum, but Matter can get you just as far. In games where skill is the deciding factor, it can even get you further. (By cheating!)<br /> <br /> A dice game can be won by Fate. Or by Matter just changing the weight distribution of the dice during your throw.<br /> <br /> Fate can lead you to the right Blackjack table, or you can use Matter to mark cards in an imperceptible way while you're playing, using some Knowing spell to make out the card marks, gradually gaining full knowledge of the deck as you go.<br /> <br /> Slot machines are of course trivially easy.<br /> <br /> Change the weight/slickness on those coins in those machines where you toss in coins that then have to push other coins out (yes, knowing the name of this machine would be useful right about now) to score big.<br /> <br /> Any Matter mage can be a professional casino player just as easy as any Fate mage can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T15:09:54-07:00","id":1121043,"title":"","content":"Fair point. I don't even think you need to mark the cards; surely a Matter Knowing spell could tell you what's on the other side of a material object in your field of view?<br /> <br /> As usual though you'll want to be careful with that, since going around openly winning every slot machine and playing Blackjack as if you know every card before it's drawn is going to make the house realize you're cheating <i>somehow</i>, even if they can't figure it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T16:58:22-07:00","id":1121092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1121043#post1121043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair point. I don't even think you need to mark the cards; surely a Matter Knowing spell could tell you what's on the other side of a material object in your field of view?</div> </div> </div> </div>A mage can also see through their familiar's senses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T01:47:22-07:00","id":1121226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1121043#post1121043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair point. I don't even think you need to mark the cards; surely a Matter Knowing spell could tell you what's on the other side of a material object in your field of view?<br /> <br /> As usual though you'll want to be careful with that, since going around openly winning every slot machine and playing Blackjack as if you know every card before it's drawn is going to make the house realize you're cheating <i>somehow</i>, even if they can't figure it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, marking does seem superfluous. And yes, be careful with it. Lose enough to draw as little attention as possible. There are professional casino players after all, mostly in the card games. Poker would probably be a good game to get into. Luck is a part of it, you won't manage to win a hand against a confident pro with good cards who has read the odds right, so you don't even have to try in order to have plenty of hands where you can lose a bit/are forced to fold. But knowing all the cards should easily help enough that you get ahead over time.<br /> <br /> Moros also tend to have high Composure in the fluff, so poker face away!<br /> <br /> Also, get a routine of using Knowing on all those scratch card lottery tickets you come across in various shops, pick out the ones that are net wins. Should build up a little bit of money from that at least. I mean, just go out and find 1-2 winning tickets for a &quot;Win for Life&quot; lottery game and you basically get a Resources 3 living standard. :P Or don't go look for them, see it as a potential extra whenever you go shopping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 07-27-2017, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T01:58:45-07:00","id":1121228,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking about becoming an investor or broker in Wall Street, using Fate to divinate the best choices to put your money or to subtly curse the competition. <br /> Considering the complexities of the Market, it would be easy to explain your success as savviness or sheer luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T03:47:58-07:00","id":1121247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1121228#post1121228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking about becoming an investor or broker in Wall Street, using Fate to divinate the best choices to put your money or to subtly curse the competition.<br /> Considering the complexities of the Market, it would be easy to explain your success as savviness or sheer luck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, so long as you have no ties to companies going up or down, even if they check into it they'll probably conclude no foul play. But they won't look into it, that's the stock market for you.<br /> <br /> It will take time to mature, though. You won't put money in and get it double tomorrow. And you need some starting capital, but with Fate that shouldn't be an issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 07-27-2017, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T10:57:03-07:00","id":1121394,"title":"","content":"I was discussing this with a friend and realized that Forces could easily make someone the best Firefighter ever. Especially if you add a dot of life or three.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T11:07:37-07:00","id":1121404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107405-making-money-with-magic?p=1107664#post1107664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather than make money using ghosts as a medium, you could go the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Necroscope\" target=\"_blank\">Necroscope</a> way. Many of the worlds dead are authors, artists, academics and so forth. One could use them to continue their work and profit off of it. Since you can make a ghost of a living person you wouldn't even necessarily need to find a dead one.<br /> <br /> Others might have knowledge of hidden treasures. Find the lost Axis gold or mineral veins or petroleum deposits.</div> </div> </div> </div>So one could say that the mage is getting a ghostwriter? <br /> <br /> <div clas